WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:06.877
The

2
00:01:05.777 --> 00:01:09.357
I'm going to go.

3
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:46.397
Hey, Hank.

4
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:49.737
Oh, hello, Sheriff.

5
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:51.697
Storm's making me a little bit nervous.

6
00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.277
I've been jumpy all night.

7
00:01:53.357 --> 00:01:55.117
The time's staged, though.

8
00:01:55.197 --> 00:01:59.668
Oh, long about midnight, but the wrecking
of the storm will hold it up some.

9
00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:03.497
They'd have to wait here to storm it over.

10
00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:05.017
Got a room?

11
00:02:05.377 --> 00:02:06.477
I've been riding all night.

12
00:02:06.557 --> 00:02:09.437
I want to get a little
sleep before stage gets in.

13
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:12.697
Expecting trouble? I'm
always expecting trouble.

14
00:02:13.597 --> 00:02:17.009
We see that place around here
where I can watch goings on.

15
00:02:17.517 --> 00:02:18.817
I got it.

16
00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:20.697
My room.

17
00:02:20.777 --> 00:02:22.277
You see that, Doc O?

18
00:02:22.357 --> 00:02:23.337
Yeah.

19
00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:25.977
Well, all you got to do is
pull it around just to one side,

20
00:02:26.057 --> 00:02:28.877
and you can see it's putting
every corner of this room.

21
00:02:28.957 --> 00:02:31.369
Cracky say, that's getting made to order.

22
00:02:31.657 --> 00:02:33.057
Call me when the stage is in.

23
00:02:33.137 --> 00:02:34.937
Will you, Hank? I'll ring the night bell.

24
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:36.137
There's two beds up there.

25
00:02:36.217 --> 00:02:38.117
Take which one you want. Good night, Hank.

26
00:02:38.197 --> 00:02:39.197
Good night.

27
00:02:42.897 --> 00:02:44.757
When is there? What a night.

28
00:02:57.937 --> 00:03:00.957
Come on.

29
00:03:41.557 --> 00:03:43.517
Oh, my God.

30
00:04:07.577 --> 00:04:09.577
I want a room with a stove in it.

31
00:04:09.657 --> 00:04:13.777
I'm chilling now, and I've got
to steep me a cup of hot tea.

32
00:04:13.857 --> 00:04:16.681
Well, there's a coal oil
of stone in every room.

33
00:04:17.297 --> 00:04:18.577
Here's your tea.

34
00:04:39.497 --> 00:04:40.717
Just sign Mr.

35
00:04:40.797 --> 00:04:42.317
and Mrs. right there.

36
00:04:49.237 --> 00:04:53.237
I suppose you folks would
like the bridal chamber?

37
00:05:03.997 --> 00:05:08.337
How much? Well, we always get
two dollars for the bridal change.

38
00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:11.357
You see, it's the best in the house.

39
00:05:15.077 --> 00:05:17.837
And please be as quiet as you can.

40
00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.537
The man next to you gets up at five.

41
00:05:35.837 --> 00:05:37.097
Hello, Hank.

42
00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:41.055
I'm putting the bottom of the light.

43
00:05:43.777 --> 00:05:45.483
Lock that up, will you, Hank?

44
00:05:45.977 --> 00:05:47.717
4,000 in there.

45
00:05:48.337 --> 00:05:50.077
Hello, I lost my mind.

46
00:05:50.157 --> 00:05:53.922
Well, it'd be safe here. It has
to take away the safe to get it.

47
00:06:20.377 --> 00:06:22.537
Good morning, Frank.

48
00:06:41.417 --> 00:06:43.497
Well, speak up, young man.

49
00:06:43.577 --> 00:06:44.577
What is it?

50
00:06:45.197 --> 00:06:46.937
I can't find it.

51
00:06:47.557 --> 00:06:48.997
You can't?

52
00:06:49.137 --> 00:06:50.257
Nope.

53
00:06:51.097 --> 00:06:53.257
Well, whatever have you lost?

54
00:06:53.597 --> 00:06:55.437
I ain't lost nothing.

55
00:06:56.197 --> 00:06:57.337
Well.

56
00:06:57.937 --> 00:07:01.957
What in the world is
it that you can't find?

57
00:07:02.037 --> 00:07:03.377
Well, it's...

58
00:07:03.457 --> 00:07:04.617
Mr.

59
00:07:04.697 --> 00:07:06.217
Oh, that's it.

60
00:07:06.477 --> 00:07:08.257
Oh, that's it.

61
00:07:22.617 --> 00:07:25.877
I tell you, Sheriff,
it's great to be young.

62
00:07:27.397 --> 00:07:28.637
Well, Hank,

63
00:07:28.857 --> 00:07:30.916
I reckon I had my trip for nothing.

64
00:07:31.257 --> 00:07:34.697
See, I was just off a
pokey-duck bandit hereabout.

65
00:07:34.777 --> 00:07:37.917
Well, you don't expect him out
in a storm like this, will you?

66
00:07:37.997 --> 00:07:41.317
You can expect him anywhere there's money.

67
00:07:42.597 --> 00:07:44.177
So, maybe.

68
00:07:59.597 --> 00:08:02.897
Thank you.

69
00:08:49.877 --> 00:08:50.597
Jerry.

70
00:08:50.677 --> 00:08:51.217
Huh?

71
00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.957
Did you hear that? No, no.

72
00:08:53.037 --> 00:08:54.697
What is it? I don't know.

73
00:09:10.237 --> 00:09:12.997
My chimney is for Pokéduck.

74
00:09:36.257 --> 00:09:38.217
I reckon your tip was right, Sheriff.

75
00:09:38.297 --> 00:09:39.897
But how'd they get the combination?

76
00:09:39.977 --> 00:09:41.217
I don't know.

77
00:09:43.397 --> 00:09:44.537
What's that?

78
00:09:46.297 --> 00:09:48.737
Well, that's a safe combination number.

79
00:09:48.957 --> 00:09:52.075
You watched it through the
window when you opened it.

80
00:10:07.297 --> 00:10:09.377
No use trying to trail him tonight.

81
00:10:09.457 --> 00:10:11.997
No. By morning, he'd be miles away.

82
00:10:12.577 --> 00:10:18.177
Just the same, I'm going to run
him down if it takes me ten years.

83
00:10:29.077 --> 00:10:32.377
Thank you.

84
00:11:00.177 --> 00:11:03.337
Thank you.

85
00:11:32.137 --> 00:11:33.397
Don't move.

86
00:11:34.817 --> 00:11:36.457
Put up your gun.

87
00:11:40.857 --> 00:11:43.077
Everything's all right, old timer.

88
00:11:43.317 --> 00:11:45.377
You're just in time for bees.

89
00:11:45.697 --> 00:11:46.717
Sit down.

90
00:11:48.937 --> 00:11:50.897
Think you're pretty slick, don't you?

91
00:11:50.977 --> 00:11:52.677
No, just careful.

92
00:11:52.837 --> 00:11:55.297
Well, you might have
been the polka dot bandit.

93
00:11:55.377 --> 00:11:57.577
Or some other notorious outlaw.

94
00:11:57.837 --> 00:11:58.837
Huh?

95
00:11:59.117 --> 00:12:00.737
Well, how do you know I ain't?

96
00:12:00.817 --> 00:12:02.437
Just by your looks.

97
00:12:02.517 --> 00:12:03.817
Come on, let's see.

98
00:12:10.657 --> 00:12:12.757
Those beans sure smell good.

99
00:12:12.837 --> 00:12:14.317
Well, help yourself.

100
00:12:25.877 --> 00:12:28.437
Pretty slick on the draw,
too, ain't you, son?

101
00:12:28.517 --> 00:12:30.817
No, old timer. Just force a habit.

102
00:12:30.897 --> 00:12:32.777
Well, don't get excited.

103
00:12:33.037 --> 00:12:34.837
See, I carry this for snakes.

104
00:12:34.917 --> 00:12:39.777
Oh, I ain't insinuating that you're
a snake, but here's to me right now.

105
00:12:39.857 --> 00:12:41.357
It's a good time to open it.

106
00:12:41.437 --> 00:12:42.537
You have a drink?

107
00:12:42.977 --> 00:12:45.497
Well, in this particular case, yes.

108
00:12:46.777 --> 00:12:49.017
You mind if I roll up here for the night?

109
00:12:49.097 --> 00:12:52.577
No, old timer. I'd be right
glad to know you better.

110
00:12:52.757 --> 00:12:53.757
Yeah?

111
00:12:54.497 --> 00:12:56.637
Well, I ain't so sure.

112
00:12:56.997 --> 00:12:59.737
Anyway, here's the mud in your eyes.

113
00:12:59.817 --> 00:13:01.077
And how.

114
00:13:25.637 --> 00:13:28.117
See any sign of Mason and the gang?

115
00:13:28.197 --> 00:13:30.637
Saw a cloud of dust down by Cotton Creek.

116
00:13:30.717 --> 00:13:32.017
Maybe the outlaws.

117
00:13:32.097 --> 00:13:33.617
Oh, are you to think so?

118
00:13:33.697 --> 00:13:36.537
How could they know when
Mason was coming through?

119
00:13:36.617 --> 00:13:38.517
Well, how did they know before?

120
00:13:38.597 --> 00:13:42.773
I tell you, there's a skunk in this
town, and we ought to run him down.

121
00:13:43.437 --> 00:13:45.417
We ought to be hearing from Sacramento.

122
00:13:45.497 --> 00:13:47.237
That letter was sent three weeks ago.

123
00:13:47.317 --> 00:13:48.337
Oh, rat.

124
00:13:48.417 --> 00:13:50.797
The government don't
care nothing about us.

125
00:13:50.877 --> 00:13:52.737
We've got to help ourselves.

126
00:13:53.117 --> 00:13:57.297
We can't fight outlaws without
ammunition, and we can get it.

127
00:14:16.137 --> 00:14:18.277
They're just entered in the pass.

128
00:14:18.477 --> 00:14:20.217
You boys know what to do.

129
00:14:20.297 --> 00:14:23.297
Remember, no harm has come to the girls.

130
00:14:39.997 --> 00:14:42.197
No sign of outlaws yet, Betty.

131
00:14:42.277 --> 00:14:45.117
But I still insist you
shouldn't have come.

132
00:14:45.197 --> 00:14:46.897
Now, don't scroll, Dad.

133
00:14:46.977 --> 00:14:48.837
It's been a wonderful trip.

134
00:14:58.177 --> 00:15:01.477
Thank you.

135
00:15:24.577 --> 00:15:25.737
Thank you.

136
00:16:13.397 --> 00:16:15.777
Sergeant, you decided
to drift along with me.

137
00:16:15.857 --> 00:16:17.817
It's kind of lonesome trailing alone.

138
00:16:17.897 --> 00:16:18.897
Yeah.

139
00:16:19.317 --> 00:16:23.057
If I ain't mistaken, you're
going to have plenty of company.

140
00:16:42.217 --> 00:16:45.537
I don't know.

141
00:17:11.077 --> 00:17:13.917
Outlaw, please help us.

142
00:17:31.857 --> 00:17:33.517
Dad!

143
00:17:42.037 --> 00:17:45.337
Come on.

144
00:18:14.837 --> 00:18:18.137
Thank you.

145
00:18:58.297 --> 00:19:00.477
Well, we got both of them.

146
00:19:00.917 --> 00:19:02.817
We'd better make sure.

147
00:19:11.077 --> 00:19:12.177
Thank you.

148
00:19:46.757 --> 00:19:48.357
No sign of them.

149
00:19:48.577 --> 00:19:50.637
I reckon they were on the bottom.

150
00:19:59.677 --> 00:20:02.265
Well, they couldn't
even got you, old-timer.

151
00:20:02.657 --> 00:20:05.357
The feel of my head, they did get me.

152
00:20:05.777 --> 00:20:06.977
What happened?

153
00:20:07.097 --> 00:20:10.803
Well, they shot you off your
horse and you fell over the cliff.

154
00:20:11.077 --> 00:20:12.637
Into the water, eh?

155
00:20:12.817 --> 00:20:14.237
You pulled me out.

156
00:20:15.097 --> 00:20:18.377
Son, I reckon I owe you my life.

157
00:20:18.657 --> 00:20:21.277
I ain't forgetting that.
Don't worry about that, Dad.

158
00:20:21.357 --> 00:20:22.857
We gotta get out of here.

159
00:20:23.157 --> 00:20:24.437
Think you can make it?

160
00:20:24.517 --> 00:20:27.937
Well, I'll make it or bust a cinch.

161
00:20:42.297 --> 00:20:43.937
Everything worked out just as you planned.

162
00:20:44.017 --> 00:20:46.077
Only we bumped into a couple of strangers.

163
00:20:46.157 --> 00:20:48.017
We had to run and fight.

164
00:20:48.097 --> 00:20:50.397
They got Jake, but they're
on the bottom of the river.

165
00:20:50.477 --> 00:20:51.637
What about the girl?

166
00:20:51.717 --> 00:20:53.477
Are you sure she didn't recognize you?

167
00:20:53.557 --> 00:20:56.137
Nah, we didn't get close enough for that.

168
00:20:56.217 --> 00:20:58.497
She's probably in town by now.

169
00:20:58.577 --> 00:20:59.577
Come on.

170
00:21:14.917 --> 00:21:16.237
Hello, boys.

171
00:21:16.317 --> 00:21:17.797
Any worries from the pack train?

172
00:21:17.877 --> 00:21:19.197
Here comes Betty now.

173
00:21:19.277 --> 00:21:21.101
That's the key out of it. Yeah.

174
00:21:36.157 --> 00:21:37.537
Where's your father?

175
00:21:38.017 --> 00:21:39.037
Where's Tom?

176
00:21:39.117 --> 00:21:40.997
Dad and Tom are dead.

177
00:21:41.077 --> 00:21:43.117
Oh, I didn't know. Who killed them?

178
00:21:43.197 --> 00:21:45.457
They killed them. Who killed them?

179
00:21:45.537 --> 00:21:48.017
There, there. Tell us
all about it, Miss Betty.

180
00:21:48.097 --> 00:21:53.577
Well, we were just coming
through the path and...

181
00:22:03.817 --> 00:22:06.317
Then these men rode after the outlaws.

182
00:22:06.537 --> 00:22:08.597
I ran to Dad and found him.

183
00:22:09.557 --> 00:22:11.357
There, there, Miss Betty.

184
00:22:11.657 --> 00:22:12.857
I am.

185
00:22:22.657 --> 00:22:25.917
Miss Betty, you must
let me take care of you.

186
00:22:25.997 --> 00:22:29.897
I want you to consider my ranch your home
until we can make more definite plans for

187
00:22:29.977 --> 00:22:30.977
your future.

188
00:22:31.057 --> 00:22:34.822
I want you to know that I'll do
everything possible to help you.

189
00:22:34.937 --> 00:22:36.977
And you'll send someone for him?

190
00:22:37.057 --> 00:22:39.557
I'm going myself, right away.

191
00:22:40.817 --> 00:22:46.017
Oh, Mrs. Williams, I want you to
take care of Betty until I return.

192
00:23:17.197 --> 00:23:19.057
In town, I reckon.

193
00:23:21.677 --> 00:23:22.697
Dead?

194
00:23:23.337 --> 00:23:25.257
Your daughter just told her.

195
00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:27.808
We were just going to bring him into town.

196
00:23:27.897 --> 00:23:28.897
Yeah?

197
00:23:29.357 --> 00:23:31.617
Well, you can give us a hand, then.

198
00:23:38.417 --> 00:23:40.157
I love the road.

199
00:23:51.257 --> 00:23:53.497
Boys, some of you take care of me.

200
00:23:53.577 --> 00:23:54.977
Come on, what happened?

201
00:23:55.117 --> 00:23:55.877
What happened?

202
00:23:55.957 --> 00:23:56.957
What

203
00:24:13.017 --> 00:24:14.117
happened?

204
00:24:14.797 --> 00:24:16.617
Don't move. Either one of you.

205
00:24:16.697 --> 00:24:18.357
Now talk and talk fast.

206
00:24:18.437 --> 00:24:20.277
Where's the rest of your
gang in the provision?

207
00:24:20.357 --> 00:24:22.197
Why was it necessary to kill?

208
00:24:24.837 --> 00:24:27.717
Men, we found these two
going through Mason's pockets.

209
00:24:27.797 --> 00:24:29.317
Now what's to be done?

210
00:24:30.377 --> 00:24:31.997
Now that's gone.

211
00:24:32.177 --> 00:24:33.717
I keep him covered.

212
00:24:34.097 --> 00:24:35.957
Men, we didn't kill Mason.

213
00:24:36.037 --> 00:24:38.037
If you'll call his
daughter, she'll prove it.

214
00:24:38.117 --> 00:24:41.057
His daughter's in no condition to
be dragged out here and questioned.

215
00:24:41.137 --> 00:24:43.677
We're not trying to question anyone,
but under the circumstances,

216
00:24:43.757 --> 00:24:45.517
I think Miss Mason
will be glad to explain.

217
00:24:45.597 --> 00:24:47.177
Here she comes now.

218
00:24:48.797 --> 00:24:51.797
Miss Mason, these men have
accused us of killing your father.

219
00:24:51.877 --> 00:24:53.497
Oh, no, Mr. Melrose.

220
00:24:53.577 --> 00:24:56.957
These are the men that drove the
outlaws away and saved my life.

221
00:24:57.037 --> 00:25:00.877
Well, in that case, we certainly
owe you gentlemen apologies.

222
00:25:01.297 --> 00:25:05.637
You, of course, don't realize, but
this town is in a most desperate state.

223
00:25:05.717 --> 00:25:10.577
We are without food and ammunition,
terrorized by a band of murdering outlaws.

224
00:25:10.717 --> 00:25:14.397
Two attempts have been made now to bring
in supplies, only to have our men killed

225
00:25:14.477 --> 00:25:16.157
and the food taken.

226
00:25:16.237 --> 00:25:20.097
If we don't get provisions here
before snow sets in, we're trapped.

227
00:25:20.177 --> 00:25:23.977
We're trapped now. We can
only last a few days longer.

228
00:25:24.057 --> 00:25:27.057
Let's all get out.
A teller is the only solution.

229
00:25:27.137 --> 00:25:28.537
I think you're right.

230
00:25:28.617 --> 00:25:33.237
How can we get out when our money is
all gone for food that we never got?

231
00:25:33.397 --> 00:25:36.737
Then I have a little money,
not much, but I'll do this.

232
00:25:36.817 --> 00:25:40.397
In order that we can get out, I'll
give you $100 each for your homestead.

233
00:25:40.477 --> 00:25:44.097
I'm taking a long chance of ever
getting my money back, but I'll risk it.

234
00:25:44.177 --> 00:25:46.357
Oh, that's my squirt, Melrose.

235
00:25:46.437 --> 00:25:47.617
Come on, let's go.

236
00:25:47.697 --> 00:25:48.717
Let's go.

237
00:25:49.077 --> 00:25:50.077
Let's go.

238
00:25:51.297 --> 00:25:54.437
Don't you think before you sell your homes
for a few dollars that you should take at

239
00:25:54.517 --> 00:25:57.537
least one more chance at
getting the provisions through?

240
00:25:57.617 --> 00:25:59.597
Our men have families.

241
00:25:59.677 --> 00:26:01.517
There's been enough killing.

242
00:26:02.157 --> 00:26:05.017
That's right. Why not
let us take a crack at it?

243
00:26:05.097 --> 00:26:07.697
If you can get us provisions,
I'll pay you well.

244
00:26:07.777 --> 00:26:08.937
Forget that.

245
00:26:09.017 --> 00:26:12.917
You give us an order and we'll have the
provisions back here inside of four days.

246
00:26:12.997 --> 00:26:13.637
Good.

247
00:26:13.717 --> 00:26:16.677
Then come to my ranch this afternoon
and I'll give you an order for a thousand

248
00:26:16.757 --> 00:26:18.177
dollar supply. That's right.

249
00:26:18.257 --> 00:26:19.257
Get out!

250
00:26:20.257 --> 00:26:21.717
Get out!

251
00:26:32.237 --> 00:26:34.457
See that pal of Melgrove?

252
00:26:35.077 --> 00:26:37.637
You're gonna be mighty
interested in him right soon.

253
00:26:37.717 --> 00:26:38.737
Who is it?

254
00:26:38.997 --> 00:26:41.057
Keeping that for a surprise.

255
00:26:41.617 --> 00:26:42.617
Huh?

256
00:26:42.817 --> 00:26:45.557
Well, I'm keeping a surprise for you, too.

257
00:26:49.037 --> 00:26:50.137
Come on.

258
00:26:50.697 --> 00:26:51.777
Come on.

259
00:27:13.577 --> 00:27:15.097
Show Miss Mason the spare room.

260
00:27:15.177 --> 00:27:16.177
Yes, senor.

261
00:27:25.457 --> 00:27:28.237
Remember, this is to be your home, Betty.

262
00:27:28.637 --> 00:27:32.477
It's going to be a great
pleasure to have you with me.

263
00:27:51.497 --> 00:27:54.157
I thought you said those two men
were at the bottom of the river.

264
00:27:54.237 --> 00:27:56.797
I'd swear those were the two we shot down.

265
00:27:57.217 --> 00:27:58.837
That's been for those two meddlers.

266
00:27:58.917 --> 00:28:00.577
The town would be moving out right now.

267
00:28:00.657 --> 00:28:02.737
Well, anyway, you got the girl.

268
00:28:02.817 --> 00:28:05.437
And remember this. She's private property.

269
00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:06.537
Hands off.

270
00:28:06.617 --> 00:28:09.337
Yeah, you better tell the boys
not to be talking around here.

271
00:28:09.417 --> 00:28:11.737
She might find out who you really are.

272
00:28:11.817 --> 00:28:14.137
Kent made another inspection
of Homestead Valley.

273
00:28:14.217 --> 00:28:17.452
Swear it'll be the richest
gold strike ever discovered.

274
00:28:19.657 --> 00:28:21.617
We'll soon be rid of those hombres.

275
00:28:21.697 --> 00:28:25.057
The town will move out and
we'll own the gold field.

276
00:28:35.797 --> 00:28:37.497
Take her to the hideout.

277
00:28:37.577 --> 00:28:39.757
We'll keep her there
till the town is deserted.

278
00:28:39.837 --> 00:28:41.297
You don't dare.

279
00:29:06.497 --> 00:29:09.203
I'm going over to Melgrove
and get that order.

280
00:29:21.957 --> 00:29:23.657
Thank you.

281
00:29:57.497 --> 00:29:59.677
Thank you.

282
00:30:44.277 --> 00:30:46.117
Only one came over.

283
00:30:46.417 --> 00:30:48.017
What are you doing in the bunkhouse?

284
00:30:48.097 --> 00:30:49.397
I don't know.

285
00:30:49.617 --> 00:30:51.397
But now is your chance.

286
00:30:51.477 --> 00:30:52.637
Remember,

287
00:30:52.837 --> 00:30:54.437
no shooting.

288
00:31:19.617 --> 00:31:22.137
You boys tell me where Melgrove is?

289
00:31:22.817 --> 00:31:27.077
Why, yeah, I think you'll
find him right, uh...

290
00:31:34.537 --> 00:31:36.237
Come on, get in.

291
00:31:57.317 --> 00:32:00.617
Thank you.

292
00:32:27.437 --> 00:32:29.677
Thank you.

293
00:33:45.617 --> 00:33:48.417
What's this all about?
I asked these men here.

294
00:33:49.497 --> 00:33:51.997
My boys have orders to hold all strangers.

295
00:33:52.077 --> 00:33:54.397
They didn't understand. I'm very sorry.

296
00:33:54.477 --> 00:33:56.417
Oh, that's all right, Norgro.

297
00:33:56.497 --> 00:33:58.277
We were just playing.

298
00:33:59.097 --> 00:34:01.637
Here's your order. And I wish you luck.

299
00:34:01.717 --> 00:34:02.697
When are you leaving?

300
00:34:02.777 --> 00:34:03.677
Right now.

301
00:34:03.757 --> 00:34:06.037
We expect to be back before daylight.

302
00:34:06.317 --> 00:34:09.077
You see, the outlaws won't
be expecting us that soon.

303
00:34:09.157 --> 00:34:10.897
I hope you'll get through.

304
00:34:11.697 --> 00:34:13.937
Well, it won't be our
fault if we don't, eh, Jake?

305
00:34:14.017 --> 00:34:15.477
You said it, son.

306
00:34:18.397 --> 00:34:20.657
Won't be expecting them, eh?

307
00:34:21.837 --> 00:34:23.337
They'll find out.

308
00:34:23.417 --> 00:34:27.077
It's the things we least
expect that usually happen.

309
00:34:38.117 --> 00:34:40.237
Thought we was going to Sandy.

310
00:34:40.857 --> 00:34:43.317
We're not gonna be that foolish old-timer.

311
00:34:43.397 --> 00:34:45.157
They'd be waiting for us at the pass.

312
00:34:45.237 --> 00:34:48.017
And you think Mel Grove and
Dantier were with the Elroy?

313
00:34:48.097 --> 00:34:49.277
There's no doubt about it.

314
00:34:49.357 --> 00:34:50.828
Well, what shall be done?

315
00:34:51.357 --> 00:34:55.475
Well, it all depends on what happens
between now and tomorrow morning.

316
00:34:56.597 --> 00:34:58.657
What happened to Miss Mason?

317
00:35:21.437 --> 00:35:24.257
Thank you.

318
00:35:49.517 --> 00:35:51.817
Thank you.

319
00:37:02.697 --> 00:37:05.057
And the tail goes with a high.

320
00:37:09.017 --> 00:37:11.899
We'll leave it gone.
They'll be coming too early.

321
00:37:13.497 --> 00:37:15.697
Where's the girl? In the strong room.

322
00:37:15.777 --> 00:37:17.857
She won't eat. She'll get over that.

323
00:37:17.937 --> 00:37:19.996
I'll have a talk with her tomorrow.

324
00:37:23.997 --> 00:37:25.357
Miss Mason?

325
00:37:28.317 --> 00:37:29.277
Betty?

326
00:37:29.357 --> 00:37:31.417
Oh, I'm so glad you found me.

327
00:37:31.497 --> 00:37:33.097
Tell me briefly what's happened.

328
00:37:33.177 --> 00:37:35.837
They caught me over here in
their plans and brought me here.

329
00:37:35.917 --> 00:37:39.497
Noguo is the leader. He's trying to force
the people out so he can get their land.

330
00:37:39.577 --> 00:37:40.577
But why?

331
00:37:40.657 --> 00:37:43.297
Well, you see, under their
topsoil is a rich gold deposit.

332
00:37:43.377 --> 00:37:45.697
And it runs right through all the ranches.

333
00:37:45.777 --> 00:37:47.197
Kent is in with them.

334
00:37:47.617 --> 00:37:49.441
Well, they'll be leaving early.

335
00:37:49.777 --> 00:37:51.657
shortly after dawn to get you.

336
00:37:51.737 --> 00:37:53.557
Now try and get some sleep.

337
00:37:53.877 --> 00:37:54.877
Good night.

338
00:38:03.137 --> 00:38:04.797
Wake up, old timer.

339
00:38:04.877 --> 00:38:06.377
Huh? What's the matter?

340
00:38:06.457 --> 00:38:08.877
Clean out them ears.
I got a world of news for you.

341
00:38:08.957 --> 00:38:11.437
Where you been? I followed
Melgrove to the hideout.

342
00:38:11.517 --> 00:38:12.477
Hey, that sounds interesting.

343
00:38:12.557 --> 00:38:15.457
Go on. Well, they're
holding Miss Mason present.

344
00:38:15.657 --> 00:38:19.697
And I got to talk to her and she
gave me the lowdown on the whole deal.

345
00:38:19.777 --> 00:38:20.895
Now listen to this.

346
00:39:12.697 --> 00:39:16.197
I'll be back by noon. I want
you to guard this place, boys.

347
00:39:16.317 --> 00:39:17.497
Keep your eye on the girl.

348
00:39:17.577 --> 00:39:18.957
If anybody comes,

349
00:39:19.197 --> 00:39:21.537
shoot. OK, boss.

350
00:39:50.277 --> 00:39:51.737
You try and find the wagon.

351
00:39:51.817 --> 00:39:53.137
I'll go get the girl.

352
00:40:45.837 --> 00:40:47.697
I've located the wagon and the horses.

353
00:40:47.777 --> 00:40:49.417
Good. Give me a left here.

354
00:40:50.017 --> 00:40:51.157
I'll take him.

355
00:40:51.237 --> 00:40:52.357
All right.

356
00:41:06.797 --> 00:41:07.997
Miss Nathan.

357
00:41:08.077 --> 00:41:10.371
Yes. Hurry and get ready. They've gone.

358
00:41:35.437 --> 00:41:38.737
Thank you.

359
00:42:00.577 --> 00:42:01.977
You've been tricked, Mel Grove.

360
00:42:02.057 --> 00:42:03.881
They're headed for the hideout.

361
00:42:17.037 --> 00:42:19.397
Keep back. I'm going to break this in.

362
00:42:29.297 --> 00:42:30.357
Are you ready?

363
00:42:30.437 --> 00:42:31.897
Oh, but maybe my booth.

364
00:42:31.977 --> 00:42:33.277
I'll meet you at the tunnel.

365
00:42:33.357 --> 00:42:34.437
All right.

366
00:42:46.477 --> 00:42:48.997
Hey, son, there's enough
grub in there to last a year.

367
00:42:49.077 --> 00:42:50.077
Come on.

368
00:43:13.597 --> 00:43:16.068
Now, just where do you think you're going?

369
00:43:19.777 --> 00:43:20.777
Ah!

370
00:43:20.897 --> 00:43:22.237
Ah!

371
00:44:24.457 --> 00:44:25.617
Look! Look!

372
00:44:25.697 --> 00:44:27.377
They're coming back!

373
00:44:51.337 --> 00:44:53.077
Good work, son, but we gotta hurry.

374
00:44:53.157 --> 00:44:54.333
They're coming back.

375
00:45:04.597 --> 00:45:08.009
Take that lone horse behind
those trees and race for town.

376
00:45:10.837 --> 00:45:12.037
Hey, son.

377
00:45:12.477 --> 00:45:13.817
Here's a box of dynamite.

378
00:45:13.897 --> 00:45:15.157
Might come in handy.

379
00:45:26.677 --> 00:45:30.397
I don't know.

380
00:46:07.817 --> 00:46:09.277
What happened? What's the matter?

381
00:46:09.357 --> 00:46:10.597
They took the girl.

382
00:46:10.677 --> 00:46:11.677
Nancy.

383
00:46:20.177 --> 00:46:23.477
Come on.

384
00:46:50.157 --> 00:46:54.477
I don't know.

385
00:47:55.397 --> 00:47:58.697
Come on.

386
00:48:44.237 --> 00:48:46.557
Keep going, old Hammer. I'll stop.

387
00:48:57.017 --> 00:48:58.917
Oh,

388
00:49:02.277 --> 00:49:03.277
my God.

389
00:49:33.697 --> 00:49:35.117
They've blocked us out.

390
00:49:35.197 --> 00:49:36.903
We've got to swim the narrow.

391
00:49:37.117 --> 00:49:39.999
A thousand dollars to the
man who gets that girl.

392
00:50:27.017 --> 00:50:30.317
Thank you.

393
00:51:11.477 --> 00:51:13.477
Here they come, old-timer.

394
00:51:14.097 --> 00:51:15.837
Don't miss your mark.

395
00:51:15.977 --> 00:51:18.537
Means the lives of everyone in town.

396
00:51:35.157 --> 00:51:40.737
Melgrove is the leader, and under your
topsoil is the richest goldfield ever

397
00:51:40.817 --> 00:51:42.757
discovered. Hooray!

398
00:51:43.697 --> 00:51:46.997
Boys, here comes the largest!

399
00:52:00.637 --> 00:52:01.877
Well, men,

400
00:52:02.097 --> 00:52:03.557
your troubles are all over.

401
00:52:03.637 --> 00:52:05.757
The outlaws are buried in the past.

402
00:52:07.917 --> 00:52:09.997
Tell them all about it, old-timer.

403
00:52:10.077 --> 00:52:12.317
Why, you see, sirs, we're like this.

404
00:52:15.697 --> 00:52:18.097
I don't know how I can ever repay them.

405
00:52:18.177 --> 00:52:19.817
Well, don't worry about that.

406
00:52:19.897 --> 00:52:22.977
It's all in my line of duty
as a government marshal.

407
00:52:23.257 --> 00:52:27.637
But I am leaving for Sacramento today,
and, uh, well, you don't know it,

408
00:52:27.717 --> 00:52:30.157
but, uh, you're going with me.

409
00:52:32.177 --> 00:52:33.397
Andy's dead.

410
00:52:33.637 --> 00:52:35.737
Must have got a slug
from one of his own men.

411
00:52:35.817 --> 00:52:37.757
Sheriff, congratulate me.

412
00:52:37.897 --> 00:52:39.297
May I present the future Mrs.

413
00:52:39.377 --> 00:52:40.717
John Carruthers?

414
00:52:40.937 --> 00:52:43.397
Wait a minute, young
man. You can't do this.

415
00:52:43.477 --> 00:52:44.837
You see, I know who you are.

416
00:52:44.917 --> 00:52:46.457
So does Miss Mason.

417
00:52:46.537 --> 00:52:49.117
You mean to say your words, uh, to...

418
00:52:49.197 --> 00:52:51.037
Now, see here, young fellow.

419
00:52:51.117 --> 00:52:54.677
I ain't forgetting you saved my
life for what you done for this town.

420
00:52:54.757 --> 00:52:56.937
But I got my duty to perform.

421
00:52:57.137 --> 00:52:59.197
Can't you see I got to take you in?

422
00:52:59.277 --> 00:53:02.137
Don't you realize I know
you're the polka dot?

423
00:53:02.217 --> 00:53:04.757
Why, Sheriff, you must have
seen me through the knothole.

424
00:53:04.837 --> 00:53:06.757
You're right, boy. Cracky, I did.

425
00:53:06.837 --> 00:53:08.357
But you saw the wrong man.

426
00:53:08.437 --> 00:53:10.917
The polka dot bandit
left just ahead of me.

427
00:53:10.997 --> 00:53:13.417
He left this row sticking in the floor.

428
00:53:13.497 --> 00:53:16.237
You must have seen me
just as I fixed that up.

429
00:53:16.537 --> 00:53:18.757
And that row belongs to Danny.

430
00:53:18.837 --> 00:53:19.837
Well,

431
00:53:20.237 --> 00:53:21.708
what do you make of this?

432
00:53:22.077 --> 00:53:24.957
Oh, I found those in
Dandy's room yesterday.

433
00:53:25.037 --> 00:53:26.757
Dandy's a polka dot bandit.

434
00:53:26.837 --> 00:53:29.797
There's a $5,000 reward for him, Sheriff.

435
00:53:29.997 --> 00:53:31.817
I guess it's up to you to collect it.

436
00:53:31.897 --> 00:53:35.637
Well, if Dandy's a polka
dot, who in blazes are you?

437
00:53:35.757 --> 00:53:37.937
Why, he's a United States Marshal.

438
00:53:38.017 --> 00:53:40.057
He's your man from Sacramento.

